age_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#manage-the-service","content":"Run it in the foreground","locale":"en"},"815":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-20","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#manage-the-service","content":"`zg --server off`","locale":"en"},"816":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-21","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#manage-the-service","content":"Stop the background service","locale":"en"},"817":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-22","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#manage-the-service","content":"Use foreground mode when you want the process and logs in the current terminal:","locale":"en"},"818":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-23","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#client-mode","content":"The CLI supports `direct`, `server`, and `auto` modes. Override the default `auto` mode with `ZVEC_GREP_MODE` or `--mode`:","locale":"en"},"819":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-24","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#client-mode","content":"`ZVEC_GREP_SERVER_URL` selects the service URL used by CLI clients.","locale":"en"},"820":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-25","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#mcp-toolsets","content":"`zg --server --stdio` starts or reuses the daemon and proxies MCP over stdin/stdout. The default `agent` toolset exposes only `zvec_grep_search`. Use `--mcp-toolset full` on `zg --install` or `zg --server` to also expose `zvec_grep_rg`, `zvec_grep_index`, `zvec_grep_index_drop`, `zvec_grep_index_status`, and `zvec_grep_server_status`.","locale":"en"},"821":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-26","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#listen-address-and-authentication","content":"The service listens on loopback and defaults to `127.0.0.1:7999`. Override the address when starting it explicitly:","locale":"en"},"822":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-27","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#listen-address-and-authentication","content":"Authentication is disabled by default on loopback. Use a token file or environment variable to require Bearer authentication:","locale":"en"},"823":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-28","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#listen-address-and-authentication","content":"Related settings are `ZVEC_GREP_SERVER_TOKEN`, `ZVEC_GREP_SERVER_TOKEN_FILE`, and `ZVEC_GREP_HOME`. Workspace indexes remain under `<root>/.zvec-grep/`.","locale":"en"},"824":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-29","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#listen-address-and-authentication","content":"Server logs are stored in `<home>/daemon/logs/server.log`; startup failures are recorded in `<home>/daemon/bootstrap.log`. The default home is `~/.zvec-grep`.","locale":"en"},"825":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-30","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#listen-address-and-authentication","content":"Restart the service after changing environment settings that affect its Embedding runtime.","locale":"en"},"826":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server-31","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/server#listen-address-and-authentication","content":"For current options, run `zg --help server` and `zg --help environment`. If the service does not become ready, see Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"827":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/supported-content","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/supported-content","type":"page",