lections/inspect-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-options","content":"Runtime behavior is governed by the options used when opening the collection:","locale":"en"},"1043":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-options","content":"`enable_mmap: 1/true` → Memory-mapped I/O is enabled for faster access.","locale":"en"},"1044":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-options","content":"`read_only: 0/false` → The collection is open for both reads and writes.","locale":"en"},"1045":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-path","content":"The `path` property returns the on-disk location of the collection:","locale":"en"},"1046":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/inspect#collection-path","content":"This is the same path passed to `open()`.","locale":"en"},"1047":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","type":"page","content":"Open","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","locale":"en"},"1048":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#usage","content":"Usage","locale":"en"},"1049":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#parameters","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"1050":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","content":"To open an existing collection, use the `open()` function to load it from disk.","locale":"en"},"1051":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","content":"The specified path **must point to an existing Zvec collection**. If no valid collection is found, `open()` will raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1052":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#parameters","content":"`path`: The filesystem path to the collection directory.","locale":"en"},"1053":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#parameters","content":"`option`: Settings that control runtime behavior.","locale":"en"},"1054":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#parameters","content":"`read_only`: Opens the collection in read-only mode. Attempts to write will raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1055":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#parameters","content":"Use read-only mode when sharing a collection across multiple processes — it ensures safe concurrent access without risking data corruption.","locale":"en"},"1056":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/open","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/open#parameters","content":"`enable_mmap`: Uses memory-mapped I/O for faster access (defaults to `True`). This trades slightly higher memory cache usage for improved performance.","locale":"en"},"1057":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","type":"page","content":"Optimize","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","locale":"en"},"1058":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"Why Optimization is Needed","locale":"en"},"1059":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#usage-example","content":"Usage Example","locale":"en"},"1060":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"Check Indexing Status","locale":"en"},"1061":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#when-to-call-optimize","content":"When to Call `optimize()`","locale":"en"},"1062":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","content":"The `optimize()` method **improves search performance** by building the configured vector index from vectors accumulated in a temporary flat buffer. It runs **in the background** and **does not block reads or writes**, ensuring your application remains fully responsive.","locale":"en"},"1063":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"In Zvec, newly inserted vectors are **not added directly** to the configured vector index. Instead, they are first staged in a lightweight flat index (brute-force) buffer.","locale":"en"},"1064":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"This design choice offers important benefits — but also a trade-off:","locale":"en"},"1065":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"✅ **Strengths**","locale":"en"},"1066":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"**Maximum write throughput**: Enables high-speed data ingestion.","locale":"en"},"1067":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"**Streaming inserts**: Supports real-time insertion for index types like IVF that don't natively allow incremental updates.","locale":"en"},"1068":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"⚠️ **Trade-off**","locale":"en"},"1069":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"**Slower searches over time**: As the flat buffer grows, search performance degrades.","locale":"en"},"1070":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"🔁 **Solution**","locale":"en"},"1071":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"Call `optimize()` periodically. This triggers a background worker that merges the staged vectors into the configured vector index — **without interrupting ongoing reads or writes**. 🚀","locale":"en"},"1072":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#why-optimization-is-needed","content":"`optimize()` **does not lock the collection**. Other threads and operations can continue reading, writing, and querying without delay while optimization is running — your application stays fully responsive.","locale":"en"},"1073":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"Use the `stats` property to get real-time insights into your collection's indexing state:","locale":"en"},"1074":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"`doc_count`: Total number of documents currently stored.","locale":"en"},"1075":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"`index_completeness`: Fraction (0.0\\~1.0) indicating how much of the vector data has been indexed.","locale":"en"},"1076":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"`1.0` → All vectors for that vector field are fully indexed using the configured index","locale":"en"},"1077":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"`0.0` → No indexing has occurred; all vectors remain in the flat buffer and are searched via brute force","locale":"en"},"1078":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#check-indexing-status","content":"**Values in between** → Indexing is partial or in progress","locale":"en"},"1079":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#when-to-call-optimize","content":"Optimize **regularly — but not too often**:","locale":"en"},"1080":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#when-to-call-optimize","content":"**Too infrequent** → Flat buffers grow large, degrading search performance","locale":"en"},"1081":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#when-to-call-optimize","content":"**Too frequent** → Wastes resources optimizing small batches prematurely","locale":"en"},"1082":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#when-to-call-optimize","content":"Find a balance based on your **data ingestion rate** and **query latency requirements**.","locale":"en"},"1083":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/optimize#when-to-call-optimize","content":"**Best practice:**\\\nCheck your collection's indexing status if searches feel slow.\\\nAs a general guideline, consider optimizing when you have **100,000+ unindexed documents** — but adjust based on your specific use case.","locale":"en"},"1084":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"page","content":"Schema Evolution","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Collections"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","locale":"en"},"1085":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"Data Definition Language (DDL)","locale":"en"},"1086":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"1087":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#column-ddl","content":"Column DDL","locale":"en"},"1088":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"Add a Column","locale":"en"},"1089":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-a-column","content":"Drop a Column","locale":"en"},"1090":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#alter-a-column","content":"Alter a Column","locale":"en"},"1091":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#view-the-current-schema","content":"View the Current Schema","locale":"en"},"1092":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#index-ddl","content":"Index DDL","locale":"en"},"1093":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"Create an Index","locale":"en"},"1094":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-an-index","content":"Drop an Index","locale":"en"},"1095":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"Zvec supports **dynamic schema evolution**, allowing you to modify a collection's structure after it has been created — without downtime, data re-ingestion, or reindexing.","locale":"en"},"1096":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"You can:","locale":"en"},"1097":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"✅ **Add or drop scalar fields**","locale":"en"},"1098":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"✅ **Rename fields** or **change their data types** ((as long as the change is safe — e.g., from `INT32` to `INT64`)","locale":"en"},"1099":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"✅ **Create or drop indexes on fields**","locale":"en"},"1100":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","content":"❌  Add or drop vector fields (🔜 coming soon)","locale":"en"},"1101":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"In Zvec, schema changes are performed using &#x2A;*Data Definition Language (DDL)** methods, grouped into two categories:","locale":"en"},"1102":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Column DDL**: defines *what data you store*.\\\nIt manages the structure of your collection by adding, removing, renaming or altering fields.","locale":"en"},"1103":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Index DDL**: defines *how you search that data*.\\\nIt controls the creation and removal of indexes on fields.","locale":"en"},"1104":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"💡 **Indexing Rules in Zvec**","locale":"en"},"1105":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Every vector field must be indexed** using an appropriate vector index to enable similarity search.","locale":"en"},"1106":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#data-definition-language-ddl","content":"**Scalar fields are optionally indexed** — but you should build inverted indexes on any scalar field you plan to use in filtering queries (e.g., `WHERE category = 'music'`).","locale":"en"},"1107":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes you have opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1108":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#prerequisites","content":"This example collection includes a scalar field `publish_year`.","locale":"en"},"1109":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"To add a new scalar field to an existing collection, use `add_column()`:","locale":"en"},"1110":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"`field_schema`:\\\nDefines the name and data type of the new field. See scalar field schema for details.","locale":"en"},"1111":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"`expression`:\\\nSpecifies the default value for existing documents. Since they don't already have a `rating` field, Zvec uses this `expression` to fill in the missing values — in this case, setting `rating = 5` for all current documents.","locale":"en"},"1112":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#add-a-column","content":"Currently, only **numerical scalar fields** can be added via `add_column()`. Support for `string` and `boolean` types is coming soon.\\\nAccordingly, the `expression` must evaluate to a number — it can be a single numerical literal (like `\"5\"`) or a simple arithmetic expression involving existing numerical fields (e.g., `\"publish_year + 1\"`).","locale":"en"},"1113":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-a-column","content":"To permanently remove a scalar field, use `drop_column()`:","locale":"en"},"1114":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#drop-a-column","content":"This **deletes the field and all its data from every document** in the collection. The operation is **irreversible**.","locale":"en"},"1115":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#alter-a-column","content":"To rename a column or update its schema, use `alter_column()`:","locale":"en"},"1116":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#view-the-current-schema","content":"After making changes, you can always check your collection's current structure by printing its schema:","locale":"en"},"1117":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#view-the-current-schema","content":"See schema example for more details.","locale":"en"},"1118":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"To accelerate search performance, you can create (or replace) indexes on both **vector** and **scalar** fields using `create_index()`:","locale":"en"},"1119":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"**Vector fields** must use one of the following index types:","locale":"en"},"1120":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`HnswIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1121":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`HnswRabitqIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1122":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`IVFIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"1123":{"id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/collections/schema-evolution#create-an-index","content":"`FlatIndexParam`","locale":"en"},"112