ndex#how-does-it-work","content":"\"Find all Italian recipes\" → look up \"Italian\" in the `cuisine` index → `[1, 4, 5]`","locale":"en"},"1452":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-77","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"\"Show recipes by Marco Rossi\" → look up \"Marco Rossi\" in the `author` index → `[4, 5]`","locale":"en"},"1453":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-78","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"\"Find Italian recipes by Julia Chen\" → intersect `[1, 4, 5]` and `[1, 6]` → `[1]`","locale":"en"},"1454":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-79","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"We **do not index** `url`, because it's rarely used in queries. Indexing it would waste storage and slow down writes, with little benefit. Once we have a document ID, we can always fetch its `url` directly from the original data.","locale":"en"},"1455":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-80","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Because it inverts the standard mapping:","locale":"en"},"1456":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-81","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Direction","locale":"en"},"1457":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-82","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Mapping","locale":"en"},"1458":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-83","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Forward","locale":"en"},"1459":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-84","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Document ID → List of Terms","locale":"en"},"1460":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-85","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Inverted","locale":"en"},"1461":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-86","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Term → List of Document IDs","locale":"en"},"1462":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-87","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"This inversion is what makes keyword-based search efficient. Instead of checking every document to see if it contains your query term, you jump straight to the term and get all matching documents immediately.","locale":"en"},"1463":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-88","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"While powerful, inverted indexes come with costs:","locale":"en"},"1464":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-89","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Storage overhead**: The index requires additional storage space.","locale":"en"},"1465":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-90","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Write amplification**: Every write operation — `INSERT`, `UPSERT`, and `UPDATE` — require index maintenance, which adds latency to writes and increases I/O load.","locale":"en"},"1466":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"page","content":"Vector Embedding","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","locale":"en"},"1467":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","content":"A numerical representation of unstructured data that captures semantic meaning for similarity search.","locale":"en"},"1468":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"What is a Vector?","locale":"en"},"1469":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"How Do You Use Vectors with a Database?","locale":"en"},"1470":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"How Vectors Power Real-World Applications?","locale":"en"},"1471":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"What is an Embedding Model?","locale":"en"},"1472":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#types-of-vectors","content":"Types of Vectors","locale":"en"},"1473":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"Dense Vectors","locale":"en"},"1474":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1475":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"In the context of AI and vector databases, &#x2A;**a vector is a list of numbers generated by embedding models to capture the semantic essence of unstructured data*** —  such as text, images, or audio.","locale":"en"},"1476":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"These models transform raw input into a high-dimensional space where &#x2A;**semantically similar items produce similar vectors***, enabling AI systems to compare meaning rather than relying on exact word matches.","locale":"en"},"1477":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"🗂️ **Store**: Generate embeddings from your data — documents, product images, or user profiles — and save them in the vector database.","locale":"en"},"1478":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"🔍 **Search**: When a new query arrives (a question, photo, etc.), generate a **query vector** using the same embedding model, then ask the database to find the most similar vectors.","locale":"en"},"1479":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"Using efficient indexes, the database quickly returns relevant results — even at large scale. This is the foundation of semantic search: **finding what &#x2A;**means**&#x2A; the same, not just what &#x2A;**says*** the same**.","locale":"en"},"1480":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"**Image search** is a great example:","locale":"en"},"1481":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"Each image is converted into a vector that captures its visual features — such as shape, color, and object type.","locale":"en"},"1482":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"Images that are **visually or semantically similar end up with nearby vectors**.","locale":"en"},"1483":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"By comparing these vectors, search systems can:","locale":"en"},"1484":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"✅ **Recognize the same person across different photos**: Even with changes in lighting, pose, or expression, images of one individual generate similar vectors, allowing the system to match identities reliably.","locale":"en"},"1485":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"✅ **Find look-alike products in e-commerce platforms**: When a user snaps a photo of a dress, lamp, or sofa, the system compares its vector to product vectors and retrieves items with similar appearance or style.","locale":"en"},"1486":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"All of this happens through fast vector similarity comparisons, powered by the vector database.","locale":"en"},"1487":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"An embedding model is an AI model that converts raw data into vector embeddings — illustrated in the diagram at the top.","locale":"en"},"1488":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"These models learn patterns from vast amounts of training data so that objects with similar meanings produce vectors that are close together in vector space — typically measured using distance metrics such as **cosine similarity**, **dot product**, or **Euclidean distance**.","locale":"en"},"1489":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"**The choice of distance metric matters.** If an embedding model was trained for a specific metric (e.g., cosine similarity), the vector database should use the same metric during search to preserve semantic relationships and achieve optimal accuracy.","locale":"en"},"1490":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"To explore and compare state-of-the-art embedding models, you can check out the Embedding Leaderboard on Hugging Face, which evaluates hundreds of models across diverse tasks and languages.","locale":"en"},"1491":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#types-of-vectors","content":"Vector representations are primarily categorized into two types: &#x2A;**dense**&#x2A; and &#x2A;**sparse***, each capturing data in its own way.","locale":"en"},"1492":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"Dense vectors are fixed-length, real-valued embeddings where (nearly) every dimension carries semantic information. These vectors are often generated by deep learning models that transform raw inputs (e.g., text, images, audio) into a structured vector space reflecting their semantic similarities.","locale":"en"},"1493":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"**✅ Semantic-Rich**: understands context and meaning (e.g., \"king – man + woman ≈ queen\")","locale":"en"},"1494":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"**⚠️ Opaque**: hard to interpret which features drive similarity","locale":"en"},"1495":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Sparse vectors are high-dimensional, often vocabulary-sized representations in which only a small subset of dimensions are non-zero. Each active dimension corresponds to a specific term (e.g., a word or n-gram), weighted by relevance scores such as **BM25**.","locale":"en"},"1496":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"In this model, every document is converted into a vector — called a document vector — that records which terms appear in it and how important they are. Similarly, a search query is also turned into a sparse vector using the same weighting scheme.","locale":"en"},"1497":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Rather than relying on exact keyword matches, similarity between a query and a document is computed using the dot product of their vectors. This measures how well their weighted terms align: documents that contain the same important terms as the query receive higher scores — rewarding both **term overlap** and **term importance**.","locale":"en"},"1498":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"For computational efficiency, sparse vectors use integer indices to map terms to their positions within a vocabulary dictionary rather than storing the term strings directly.","locale":"en"},"1499":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"**✅ Interpretable**: non-zero dimensions map directly to known terms (e.g., `4017` → \"puppy\")","locale":"en"},"1500":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"**⚠️ Lacks Semantic Understanding**: treats \"car\" and \"automobile\" as unrelated unless explicitly linked","locale":"en"},"1501":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"page","content":"Delete","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","locale":"en"},"1502":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Delete by IDs","locale":"en"},"1503":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"Delete by Filter Condition","locale":"en"},"1504":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Zvec provides two ways to delete documents. Choose the method that best fits your use case:","locale":"en"},"1505":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"1506":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Input","locale":"en"},"1507":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"When to Use","locale":"en"},"1508":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"`delete()`","locale":"en"},"1509":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"One or more document `id`s","locale":"en"},"1510":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Use when you know the exact ID(s) of the documents you want to delete","locale":"en"},"1511":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"`delete_by_filter()`","locale":"en"},"1512":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"A filter expression (e.g., `publish_year < 1900`)","locale":"en"},"1513":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Use for bulk deletion based on field values — ideal for cleaning up documents that match specific criteria","locale":"en"},"1514":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Delete operations are **immediate** and **irreversible**.\\\nAlways double-check your input before running a delete operation.","locale":"en"},"1515":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Assume you've already opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1516":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Use `delete()` to remove one or more documents when you know their exact IDs.","locale":"en"},"1517":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"When given a single `id`, `delete()` returns one `Status` object.","locale":"en"},"1518":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"When given a list of `id`s, it returns a list of `Status` objects in the same order.","locale":"en"},"1519":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"Use `delete_by_filter()` to remove all documents that match a boolean `filter` expression.","locale":"en"},"1520":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"The `filter` can reference scalar fields (e.g., `publish_year`, `language`) using comparison and logical operators.","locale":"en"},"1521":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","type":"page","content":"Fetch","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","locale":"en"},"1522":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"Use `fetch()` to retrieve documents by their `id`s.\\\nThis is a **direct lookup** — no search, scoring, or filtering is involved.","locale":"en"},"1523":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"**Input**: A single document `id` or a list of document `id`s.","locale":"en"},"1524":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"**Output**: A mapping from each **found** `id` to its corresponding document object.","locale":"en"},"1525":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"Missing `id`s are **silently omitted** from the result (no error raised).","locale":"en"},"1526":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"The returned dictionary does not guarantee input order — access documents by `id` instead.","locale":"en"},"1527":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","type":"page","content":"Data Operations","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","locale":"en"},"1528":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Zvec provides a complete set of **data manipulation operations** to manage documents in your collection.","locale":"en"},"1529":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"1530":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"1531":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Insert`","locale":"en"},"1532":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Add new documents (fails if the document `ID` already exists)","locale":"en"},"1533":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Upsert`","locale":"en"},"1534":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Insert new documents or replace existing ones by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1535":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Update`","locale":"en"},"1536":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Modify specific fields of existing documents by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1537":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Delete`","locale":"en"},"1538":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Delete documents by `ID` or using a scalar filter condition","locale":"en"},"1539":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Query`","locale":"en"},"1540":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Perform vector similarity search or full-text search, optionally combined with scalar filtering and re-ranking","locale":"en"},"1541":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Fetch`","locale":"en"},"1542":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Retrieve full documents directly by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1543":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Iterate`","locale":"en"},"1544":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Stream every document one by one without loading the whole collection into memory","locale":"en"},"1545":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"All write operations (`insert`, `upsert`, `update`, `delete`) are immediately visible for querying — enabling true real-time, streaming workloads.","locale":"en"},"1546":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"page","content":"Insert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","locale":"en"},"1547":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1548":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Insert a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1549":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Insert a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1550":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert Documents with Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1551":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert Documents with Multiple Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1552":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","content":"Use the &#x2A;*`insert()`** method to add one or more new documents (`Doc`) to a collection.","locale":"en"},"1553":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","content":"**Performance Tip**:\\\nNew vectors are initially buffered for fast ingestion. For optimal search performance, call `optimize()` after inserting a large batch of documents.","locale":"en"},"1554":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `insert()` must:","locale":"en"},"1555":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Have a unique `id` (not already present in the collection)","locale":"en"},"1556":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Provide data that matches the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1557":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"**Scalar fields**: provided as key–value pairs under `fields` (scalar field names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1558":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"**Vector embeddings**: provided as key–value pairs under `vectors` (vector names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1559":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"You can omit `nullable` scalar fields if a document doesn't have a value for them","locale":"en"},"1560":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"If a document with the same `id` already exists in the collection, the insertion will **fail** for that document.\\\nTo overwrite existing documents or insert without checking, use `upsert()` instead.","locale":"en"},"1561":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Assume you already have a collection with the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1562":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A scalar field: `text` (string)","locale":"en"},"1563":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A dense vector embedding: `text_embedding` (4-dimensional FP32 vector)","locale":"en"},"1564":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The 4-dimensional vector is for demonstration only — real-world embeddings are usually much larger.","locale":"en"},"1565":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"You've also opened the collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1566":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Now, insert a document like this:","locale":"en"},"1567":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The `insert()` method validates the document first:","locale":"en"},"1568":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"**Incorrect usage** — such as an unknown field or wrong vector dimension — **raises an error**.","locale":"en"},"1569":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"**If validation passes**, the method proceeds with the insertion and returns a `Status` object indicating success or failure (e.g., duplicate `ID`, insufficient disk space).","locale":"en"},"1570":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Successfully inserted documents are immediately available for querying 🚀.","locale":"en"},"1571":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"To insert multiple documents at once, pass a list of `Doc` objects to `insert()`.\\\nEach `Doc` is processed independently, and the method returns a list of `Status` objects — one per document.","locale":"en"},"1572":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are inserted**.","locale":"en"},"1573":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to insert every one. A failure in one (e.g., duplicate `id`) does **not** stop others from being inserted.","locale":"en"},"1574":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1575":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Assume your collection includes a sparse vector named `sparse_embedding`.","locale":"en"},"1576":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert a document with a sparse vector like this:","locale":"en"},"1577":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"A sparse vector is represented as a mapping from `dimension indices` (integers) to `values` (floats).\\\nThere is **no fixed dimension size** — only non-zero dimensions need to be included.","locale":"en"},"1578":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Real-world applications often require collections with multiple scalar fields and vector embeddings. In this example, assume your collection includes the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1579":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1580":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`book_title` (string)","locale":"en"},"1581":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`category` (array of strings)","locale":"en"},"1582":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`publish_year` (32-bit integer)","locale":"en"},"1583":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Vector embeddings**:","locale":"en"},"1584":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`dense_embedding`: a 768-dimensional dense vector","locale":"en"},"1585":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`sparse_embedding`: a sparse vector","locale":"en"},"1586":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert a document with multiple fields and vectors like this:","locale":"en"},"1587":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"page","content":"Iterate","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","locale":"en"},"1588":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"Select Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1589":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Snapshot Semantics","locale":"en"},"1590":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Concurrency","locale":"en"},"1591":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Break Early","locale":"en"},"1592":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Use &#x2A;*`iter_docs()`** to stream **all** documents in a collection one by one.","locale":"en"},"1593":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Unlike `fetch()` — which retrieves documents by known `id`s — iteration performs a **full scan**. Documents are streamed in bounded windows, so the whole collection is never materialized in memory at once — making it suitable for export, backup, migration, or offline processing.","locale":"en"},"1594":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"The iterator holds a native resource slot on the collection, so let the language close it for you: Python's `with` statement and JavaScript's `for...of` loop both release the iterator when the loop finishes, breaks early, or raises an exception. Iterators also close themselves automatically when fully exhausted.","locale":"en"},"1595":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"By default, every scalar field and every vector is materialized for each document. Use `output_fields` and `include_vector` to reduce the amount of data read:","locale":"en"},"1596":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`output_fields`** (`outputFields`): a list of scalar field names to return. If omitted, all scalar fields are returned; an empty list returns no scalar fields. Unknown or duplicate names raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1597":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`include_vector`** (`includeVector`): whether to materialize vector data. Vectors are included by default; disable it when you only need scalar fields — skipping vectors makes traversal faster.","locale":"en"},"1598":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Both `iter_docs()` and `iterDocsSync()` iterate over an **isolated snapshot taken at call time**:","locale":"en"},"1599":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Data written **after** the iterator is created — inserts, upserts, updates — is **not visible** to this iterator.","locale":"en"},"1600":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Deletes made after creation do not affect the iteration; documents already deleted when the snapshot was taken are filtered out.","locale":"en"},"1601":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"On a writable collection, creating the iterator may seal the current writing segment (each call can produce a new small segment); read-only collections are scanned directly without any write.","locale":"en"},"1602":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Iteration order is unspecified — it is **not** insertion order, and it can change after `optimize()` reorganizes segments — so never rely on it.","locale":"en"},"1603":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"While any iterator is open on a collection, these operations **raise an error**:","locale":"en"},"1604":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Schema changes — creating or dropping an index, adding, altering or dropping a column","locale":"en"},"1605":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"`optimize()`, which fails at its start","locale":"en"},"1606":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Closing or destroying the collection","locale":"en"},"1607":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Conversely, creating an iterator fails while one of those maintenance operations is already running. Writes, `flush()`, `query()` and `fetch()` remain **unaffected**.","locale":"en"},"1608":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Close every iterator before closing the collection. These restrictions are lifted as soon as all open iterators are closed.","locale":"en"},"1609":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Stopping before the end is safe — exiting the `with` block or the `for...of` loop releases the iterator's slot. When you drive the iterator manually instead, close it yourself:","locale":"en"},"1610":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"page","content":"Update","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","locale":"en"},"1611":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1612":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Update a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1613":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Update a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1614":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Use `update()` to modify **existing** documents (`Doc`).","locale":"en"},"1615":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Only the scalar fields and vector embeddings you **include will be updated**; all other content remains unchanged.","locale":"en"},"1616":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"The method accepts either a single `Doc` object or a list of `Doc` objects.","locale":"en"},"1617":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `update()` must:","locale":"en"},"1618":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Specify an `id` that **already exists** in the collection (the operation will fail if the document is not found)","locale":"en"},"1619":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Include only the fields and vectors you **intend to update**, formatted according to the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1620":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"**Scalar fields**: provided as key–value pairs under `fields` (scalar field names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1621":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"**Vector embeddings**: provided as key–value pairs under `vectors` (vector names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1622":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Omit any scalar fields or vectors you do not want to change — they will be left untouched.","locale":"en"},"1623":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Assume you already have a collection with the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1624":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1625":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`book_title` (string)","locale":"en"},"1626":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`category` (array of strings)","locale":"en"},"1627":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`publish_year` (32-bit integer)","locale":"en"},"1628":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**Vector embeddings**:","locale":"en"},"1629":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`dense_embedding`: a 768-dimensional dense vector","locale":"en"},"1630":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`sparse_embedding`: a sparse vector","locale":"en"},"1631":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"To update an existing document, provide its `id` and only the fields or vectors you want to change:","locale":"en"},"1632":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"The `update()` method validates the document first:","locale":"en"},"1633":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**Incorrect usage** — such as an unknown field or wrong vector dimension — **raises an error**.","locale":"en"},"1634":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**If validation passes**, the method proceeds with the update and returns a `Status` object indicating success or failure (e.g., non-existing `ID`).","locale":"en"},"1635":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Successfully updated documents are immediately available for querying 🚀.","locale":"en"},"1636":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"To update multiple documents at once, pass a list of `Doc` objects to `update()`.\\\nEach `Doc` is processed independently, and the method returns a list of `Status` objects — one per document.","locale":"en"},"1637":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are updated**.","locale":"en"},"1638":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to update every one. A failure in one (e.g., the `id` doesn't exist) does **not** stop others from being updated.","locale":"en"},"1639":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1640":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"page","content":"Upsert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","locale":"en"},"1641":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1642":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"Upsert a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1643":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Upsert a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1644":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Upsert Documents with Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1645":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Upsert Documents with Multiple Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1646":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"`upsert()` works similar to `insert()` — it adds one or more new documents (`Doc`) to a collection.","locale":"en"},"1647":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"The key difference is that if a document with the same `id` already exists, it will be **overwritten**.","locale":"en"},"1648":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"Use `upsert()` if you want to overwrite an existing document (or don't mind replacing it).","locale":"en"},"1649":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"Use `insert()` if you want to avoid accidentally overwriting a document — `insert()` will fail if a document with the same id already exists.","locale":"en"},"1650":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"**Performance Tip**:\\\nNew vectors are initially buffered for fast ingestion. For optimal search performance, call `optimize()` after upserting a large batch of documents.","locale":"en"},"1651":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `upsert()` must:","locale":"en"},"1652":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Have an `id` (if a document with the same `id` already exists, it will be replaced)","locale":"en"},"1653":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Provide data that matches the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1654":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"**Scalar fields**: provided as key–value pairs under `fields` (scalar field names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1655":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"**Vector embeddings**: provided as key–value pairs under `vectors` (vector names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1656":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"You can omit `nullable` scalar fields if a document doesn't have a value for them","locale":"en"},"1657":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"Assume you already have a collection with the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1658":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"A scalar field: `text` (string)","locale":"en"},"1659":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"A dense vector embedding: `text_embedding` (4-dimensional FP32 vector)","locale":"en"},"1660":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"The 4-dimensional vector is for demonstration only — real-world embeddings are usually much larger.","locale":"en"},"1661":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"You've also opened the collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1662":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"Now, upsert a document like this:","locale":"en"},"1663":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"The `upsert()` method validates the document first:","locale":"en"},"1664":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"**Incorrect usage** — such as an unknown field or wrong vector dimension — **raises an error**.","locale":"en"},"1665":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"**If validation passes**, the method proceeds with the upsertion and returns a `Status` object indicating success or failure (e.g., insufficient disk space).","locale":"en"},"1666":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"Successfully upserted documents are immediately available for querying 🚀.","locale":"en"},"1667":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"To upsert multiple documents at once, pass a list of `Doc` objects to `upsert()`.\\\nEach `Doc` is processed independently, and the method returns a list of `Status` objects — one per document.","locale":"en"},"1668":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are upserted**.","locale":"en"},"1669":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to upsert every one. A failure in one (e.g., insufficient disk space) does **not** stop others from being upserted.","locale":"en"},"1670":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1671":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Assume your collection includes a sparse vector named `sparse_embedding`.","loca