url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#jieba-tokenizer","content":"Segmentation mode: `\"search\"` (fine-grained, recommended for search), `\"mix\"`, `\"full\"`, or `\"hmm\"`. See cppjieba documentation for details on each mode.","locale":"en"},"2419":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-157","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#jieba-tokenizer","content":"Jieba uses the field's `jieba_dict_dir` first, then the `ZVEC_JIEBA_DICT_DIR` environment variable. If both are unset or empty, it uses the embedded resources. An unreadable file required by the selected mode causes initialization to fail.","locale":"en"},"2420":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-158","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"Token filters are applied in sequence after tokenization. The same filter configuration is used for both indexing and querying.","locale":"en"},"2421":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-159","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"Filter","locale":"en"},"2422":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-160","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"2423":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-161","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"`\"lowercase\"`","locale":"en"},"2424":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-162","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"Converts tokens to Unicode lowercase.","locale":"en"},"2425":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-163","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"`\"ascii_folding\"`","locale":"en"},"2426":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-164","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"Folds Unicode characters into ASCII equivalents.","locale":"en"},"2427":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-165","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"`\"stemmer\"`","locale":"en"},"2428":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-166","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"Normalizes word forms using a Snowball stemmer.","locale":"en"},"2429":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-167","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#token-filters","content":"For English text, use `lowercase` and `stemmer` so case and word forms do not affect matching. For English-like text or text with diacritics, you can also add `ascii_folding` for accent-insensitive matching.","locale":"en"},"2430":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-168","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#lowercase-filter","content":"`\"lowercase\"` converts tokens to Unicode lowercase.","locale":"en"},"2431":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-169","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#ascii-folding-filter","content":"`\"ascii_folding\"` folds Unicode characters into ASCII equivalents.","locale":"en"},"2432":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-170","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"`\"stemmer\"` normalizes word forms using a Snowball stemmer. The default language is `\"english\"`.","locale":"en"},"2433":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-171","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"**Stemmer configuration** (via `extra_params` JSON):","locale":"en"},"2434":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-172","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"2435":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-173","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"Type","locale":"en"},"2436":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-174","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"2437":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-175","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"2438":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-176","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"`stemmer_lang`","locale":"en"},"2439":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-177","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"`str`","locale":"en"},"2440":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-178","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"`\"english\"`","locale":"en"},"2441":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-179","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#stemmer-filter","content":"Snowball language or algorithm name. For example, set it to `\"porter\"` for behavior close to Elasticsearch's default English stemmer.","locale":"en"},"2442":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-180","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#constraints","content":"FTS and vector search are **mutually exclusive within one query route** — a single `Query` / `ZVecQuery` should not set both `fts` and `vector` / `id`.","locale":"en"},"2443":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-181","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#constraints","content":"`query_string` and `match_string` are **mutually exclusive** in a single `Fts` object.","locale":"en"},"2444":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-182","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#constraints","content":"Define text columns in the collection schema. The schema evolution API cannot add, alter, or drop FTS columns. Use `create_index()` or `drop_index()` to manage the index on an existing string column.","locale":"en"},"2445":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-183","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#constraints","content":"Leading negation (`NOT term` or standalone `-term`) is not supported — at least one positive term is required.","locale":"en"},"2446":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"page","content":"Grouped Search","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","locale":"en"},"2447":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#how-it-works","content":"How It Works","locale":"en"},"2448":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2449":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#performing-grouped-search","content":"Performing Grouped Search","locale":"en"},"2450":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#using-the-vector-from-an-existing-document","content":"Using the Vector from an Existing Document","locale":"en"},"2451":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2452":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#results","content":"Results","locale":"en"},"2453":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"Limitations and Considerations","locale":"en"},"2454":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","content":"Grouped search organizes vector search results by scalar field values and returns the most relevant groups, along with the most relevant documents in each group.","locale":"en"},"2455":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","content":"For example, grouping product search results by `category` prevents one category from dominating the results while preserving the most relevant products in each category.","locale":"en"},"2456":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#how-it-works","content":"When performing grouped search, Zvec:","locale":"en"},"2457":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#how-it-works","content":"Groups results during vector search by the value of the specified grouping field.","locale":"en"},"2458":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#how-it-works","content":"Ranks groups by the most relevant document in each group and returns up to the specified number of groups.","locale":"en"},"2459":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#how-it-works","content":"Keeps up to the specified number of documents in each group, ordered by relevance.","locale":"en"},"2460":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#how-it-works","content":"Documents whose grouping field is `null` are excluded from the results.","locale":"en"},"2461":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes that you have opened a collection and that:","locale":"en"},"2462":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#prerequisites","content":"The query field is a vector field with an index that supports grouped search.","locale":"en"},"2463":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#prerequisites","content":"The grouping field is a non-array scalar field, such as an integer, float, string, or boolean field.","locale":"en"},"2464":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains a dense vector field named `dense_embedding` and scalar fields used for grouping and filtering.","locale":"en"},"2465":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#performing-grouped-search","content":"Specify a single query vector, a grouping field name, the number of groups to return, and the number of documents per group:","locale":"en"},"2466":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#performing-grouped-search","content":"If fewer matching groups or documents are available, the actual result counts will be lower than `group_count` or `topk_per_group`. An empty collection or a search with no matches returns an empty list.","locale":"en"},"2467":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#using-the-vector-from-an-existing-document","content":"Instead of providing an embedding directly, you can use `id` to reuse the vector from an existing document in the collection:","locale":"en"},"2468":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#using-the-vector-from-an-existing-document","content":"The document specified by `id` must exist and contain the vector identified by `field_name`.","locale":"en"},"2469":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#using-the-vector-from-an-existing-document","content":"The Node.js API requires an explicit query `vector`.","locale":"en"},"2470":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"2471":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"Type","locale":"en"},"2472":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"2473":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"2474":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"`query`","locale":"en"},"2475":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"`Query`","locale":"en"},"2476":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"Required","locale":"en"},"2477":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"A single vector search specification. Provide an embedding through `vector`, or use `id` to reuse the vector from an existing document. You can pass index-specific query parameters through `param`.","locale":"en"},"2478":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"`group_by_field_name`","locale":"en"},"2479":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#parameters","content":"`str`","locale":"en"},"2480":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-oper